---
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CTPAT Supply Chain Security Readiness | Eurocert"
  description="Prepare for CTPAT participation and CBP validation with a readiness assessment of applicable security criteria, documented risks, controls and corrective actions. CBP determines eligibility and membership."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.eurocert.asia/social-audits/ctpat/"
  ogImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367859/eurocert/Untitled_design_19_.png.png"
  keywords="Eurocert Asia,Eurocert Asia,ISO certification,CE marking,food safety certification,FSSC 22000,BRCGS,GFSI,social audits,Sedex,SMETA,SA8000,inspection services,certification body,India,management systems,ISO 9001,ISO 14001,ISO 45001"
>
<style is:global>@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:900;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Brands";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-brands-400.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-regular-400.woff2) format('woff2')}</style>
<section class="relative min-h-[55vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[#030a16]"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/didtfhfme/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1783747209/0912abda-9285-4279-8a36-e9b196d8af45_sxju2a.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-30" alt="CTPAT Customs-Trade Partnership Against Terrorism"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#030a16]/70 via-[#030a16]/40 to-[#030a16]"></div></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10 text-center py-20"><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-eurogold-400/30 bg-eurogold-400/5 mb-6"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400 animate-pulse"></span><span class="heading-font text-[10px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-bold">Voluntary Supply Chain Security Program by U.S. Customs &amp; Border Protection</span></div><h1 class="heading-font text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-3 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,168,67,0.3)">CTPAT Supply Chain Security Readiness for Indian Exporters<!-- --> <span class="text-eurogold-400"></span></h1><p class="text-white/90 text-sm md:text-base max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Prepare to support a U.S. CTPAT participant supply chain and potential CBP validation with a structured review of risks, security controls, records, and corrective actions.</p></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">See our guides on <a class="text-euro-600 hover:underline" href="/post/ctpat-compliance-vs-validation/">CTPAT validation vs. audit</a> and <a class="text-euro-600 hover:underline" href="/post/ctpat-minimum-security-criteria/">CBP Minimum Security Criteria</a>.</p></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 items-start"><div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-6"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Program Overview</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">What is <span class="text-euro-600">CTPAT?</span></h2></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">CTPAT (Customs Trade Partnership Against Terrorism) is a voluntary U.S. supply-chain security program administered by <a class="text-euro-600 hover:underline" href="https://www.cbp.gov/border-security/ports-entry/cargo-security/ctpat" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP)</a>. It brings eligible trade partners together with CBP to identify and reduce security risks in international trade.</p><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">Eligibility is specific to the CTPAT entity type. CBP currently limits its Foreign Manufacturer category to manufacturers incorporated in Mexico or Canada; Indian exporters should confirm eligibility with CBP and their U.S. importer or CTPAT partner. Eurocert can assess supplier-side readiness but cannot enroll a business or grant CTPAT status.</p><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/40"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-handshake text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">How CTPAT Works</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">For an eligible applicant, the process begins by confirming the applicable CBP entity category and Minimum Security Criteria, documenting a supply-chain risk assessment, and completing an application and security profile in the CTPAT Portal. CBP reviews the materials, determines eligibility and membership, and conducts official validations. Indian suppliers may be asked by a U.S. CTPAT participant to provide information about site-level controls; this does not make the supplier a CTPAT member.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-2 relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-slate-100 h-[320px] md:h-[400px] group"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367934/eurocert/b9.png.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-105" alt="CTPAT Customs-Trade Partnership"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900/20 via-transparent to-transparent"></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Risk Assessment</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">The Five Step <span class="text-euro-600">Risk Assessment Process</span></h2></div><div class="space-y-4"><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300"><div class="flex items-start gap-5"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm">01</span></div><div><h4 class="heading-font text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Map Cargo/Data Flow</h4><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Map cargo/data flow and control, identify business partners (directly or indirectly contracted) and how cargo moves throughout the supply chain including modes of transportation (air, sea, rail, or truck) and nodes (country of origin, transit points).</p></div></div></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300"><div class="flex items-start gap-5"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm">02</span></div><div><h4 class="heading-font text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Conduct Threat Assessment</h4><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Focus on Terrorism, Contraband Smuggling, Human Smuggling, Agricultural and Public Safety Threats, Organized Crime, and conditions in a country/region which may foster such threats, and rank those threats.</p></div></div></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300"><div class="flex items-start gap-5"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm">03</span></div><div><h4 class="heading-font text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Conduct Vulnerability Assessment</h4><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">In accordance with CTPAT Minimum Security Criteria  -  identify what the Partner has that a terrorist or criminal might desire (data, access to cargo, company information), then identify weaknesses in procedures that would allow access.</p></div></div></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300"><div class="flex items-start gap-5"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm">04</span></div><div><h4 class="heading-font text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Prepare Written Action Plan</h4><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Address vulnerabilities with mechanisms to record identified weaknesses, who is responsible for addressing the issues, and due dates. Report results to appropriate company officials and employees on completed follow up and changes.</p></div></div></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300"><div class="flex items-start gap-5"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm">05</span></div><div><h4 class="heading-font text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Document the Procedure</h4><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Document how risk assessments are conducted, including reviewing and revising the procedure periodically. The process should be reviewed and updated at least annually, and a Risk Assessment should be conducted and documented at least annually.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#030a16]"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,rgba(212,168,67,0.06)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div><div class="relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-18"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Understanding Validation</h4><h3 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">CTPAT <span class="text-eurogold-400">Validation FAQs</span></h3></div><div class="space-y-5"><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-question text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest">What is a CTPAT Validation?</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">A CTPAT validation is a CBP-led review of a participant security profile and its implementation. CBP may meet company representatives and visit selected domestic or foreign sites to verify that described measures are accurate and followed. An Indian supplier site may be included in a member supply-chain validation, but CBP determines the scope and outcome.</p></div><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-bullseye text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest">What is the Goal of a CTPAT Validation?</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">CBP uses validation to assess whether a participant security profile is accurate, reliable, effective, and implemented. The review also allows CBP and the participant to discuss supply-chain risks and best practices. CBP determines the validation result; an independent readiness review is not an official CBP validation.</p></div><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-not-equal text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest">Is a CTPAT Validation an Audit?</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">A CTPAT validation is CBP verification of a participant security profile and its implementation. It is not the same as an independent certification audit or a general review of compliance with every customs or trade law. CBP retains its customs enforcement and inspection authority regardless of a participant status.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Updated Requirements</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">CTPAT <span class="text-euro-600">Security Focus Areas</span></h2><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4">Minimum Security Criteria vary by participant type and current CBP guidance. Depending on the applicable criteria, a readiness review may examine documented supply-chain risk assessments, business-partner controls, personnel and physical access, cargo and conveyance security, incident reporting, and cybersecurity. This is an overview, not a universal checklist. <a class="text-euro-600 hover:underline" href="https://www.cbp.gov/border-security/ports-entry/cargo-security/ctpat-customs-trade-partnership-against-terrorism/apply/security-criteria" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review CBP criteria for the relevant entity type</a>.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-6 bg-[#f8fafc] rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 shrink-0 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-user-shield text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900">Management Commitment to a Culture of Security</h4></div><div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-6 bg-[#f8fafc] rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 shrink-0 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-laptop-code text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900">Cyber Security and Protection from Social Engineering Threats</h4></div><div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-6 bg-[#f8fafc] rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 shrink-0 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-seedling text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900">Agricultural Security</h4></div><div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-6 bg-[#f8fafc] rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 shrink-0 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-money-bill-wave text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900">Prevention of Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing</h4></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Membership Benefits</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">Benefits of CTPAT <span class="text-euro-600">Membership</span></h2><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4">Program benefits are set by CBP and apply to eligible participants under current rules. A readiness assessment does not confer membership or guarantee a particular benefit.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5 max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">CTPAT Validation</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Prepare for the CBP-led validation process; only CBP can award CTPAT status.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-search text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Supply Chain Security Assessment</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Comprehensive assessment of your supply chain security practices and vulnerabilities.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-cogs text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Security Best Practices</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Implement robust security controls and best practices across your supply chain.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-shipping-fast text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Faster Customs Clearance</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Eligible participants may receive trade-facilitation benefits under current CBP rules.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-check-double text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Reduced Inspections</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Membership may reduce examination frequency, but CBP retains discretion to inspect shipments.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-star text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Priority CBP Processing</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Some eligible participants may qualify for priority processing under CBP rules.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-flag-usa text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Front-of-Line Status</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Certain eligible participants may qualify for front-of-line treatment at participating crossings.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group text-center"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 mx-auto group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-handshake text-lg"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Enhanced Trade Partnership</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Strengthen your partnership with U.S. Customs &amp; Border Protection.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#030a16]"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,rgba(212,168,67,0.06)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div><div class="relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-18"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">CTPAT Readiness Support</h4><h3 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Why Choose <span class="text-eurogold-400">CTPAT Readiness Support?</span></h3></div><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8"><div class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-building text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">About Eurocert Asia</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">Eurocert Asia provides independent readiness reviews and third-party audit services within its applicable scope. For CTPAT, our role is to assess preparedness and identify gaps; CBP alone handles program admission and official validation.</p></div><div class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-white font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">CTPAT Expertise</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Readiness support can review documented risk assessments, applicable security controls, business-partner and site-level evidence, and corrective-action plans. The scope follows the criteria applicable to the U.S. participant and relevant sites; our support does not guarantee membership or a CBP validation outcome.</p><p class="text-white/45 text-sm leading-relaxed">We help Indian suppliers prepare accurate site-level security information for a U.S. CTPAT participant and a potential CBP review. Eligibility and applicable requirements remain subject to CBP and the participant entity type.</p></div></div><div class="p-5 mt-8 rounded-xl border border-eurogold-400/20 bg-eurogold-400/5 text-center"><p class="text-white/60 text-sm leading-relaxed">Eurocert S.A. was established in Athens, Greece, in 1998. Eurocert Asia provides supplier-side readiness support; CBP retains all CTPAT program decisions.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-6"><div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-eurogold-400/20 bg-eurogold-400/5 text-center"><span class="heading-font text-eurogold-400 font-bold text-3xl block mb-1 leading-none">{SITE.metrics.countriesServed}</span><span class="text-[9px] font-bold text-white/50 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] heading-font">Countries</span></div